# Wireframe: Sidebar (App Shell — Navigation Panel)

## Purpose & Flow Context

Persistent left-side navigation panel showing primary app routes (Issues, Projects, Cycles, Settings) with current-route highlighting. Serves all authenticated flows — app shell shared across all protected pages. Entry: app renders after auth hydration. Exit: click a nav link → route changes, highlight updates.

---

## Notation Legend

| Symbol | Meaning | Symbol | Meaning |
|--------|---------|--------|---------|
| `[...]` | Button / interactive element | `[>...▼]` | Dropdown |
| `_______` | Text input / editable field | `[X]` | Close / dismiss |
| `⚠` | Warning / due date | `📎N` | N attachments |
| `💬N` | N comments | `🔗` | Card relationship |
| `👤` | User / mention | `○ ●` | Radio unselected / selected |
| `▎` | Active indicator bar | `»` | Collapse toggle |

## Accessibility — Shared Conventions

All interactive screens inherit these. Per-screen specifics noted where they diverge.

| Concern | Convention |
|---------|------------|
| Landmarks | `header`, `main`, `aside`, `contentinfo` |
| Heading order | One `h1` per screen, `h2` for sections |
| Accessible names | Icon-only controls get `aria-label` |
| Keyboard | Tab, Enter/Space, Escape, Arrow keys |
| Target size | ≥24×24 CSS px reservation |
| Non-color intent | Icon + text, never color alone |

---

## Layout Regions

**Grid**: Sidebar occupies fixed-width left column (240px expanded, 56px collapsed). App shell uses a 2-column layout: sidebar | main content.

| Region | Content | Notes |
|--------|---------|-------|
| Sidebar container | `<aside>` full-height panel | `aria-label="Main navigation"`, sticky, scrollable |
| Collapse toggle | Icon button top-right | Collapses/expands sidebar, state persisted in UI Store |
| Team selector | Dropdown at top of sidebar | Shows current team name, allows switching |
| Nav section heading | "Navigation" or similar section label | Visible in expanded state |
| Nav links | List of NavLink components | Issues, Projects, Cycles, Settings |
| Active indicator | Left accent bar on active nav link | Visually distinguishes current route |
| User menu | Avatar + name at bottom of sidebar | Click opens dropdown with profile/logout |

**Content hierarchy** (by visual priority):
1. Team selector — establishes context
2. Nav links — primary navigation actions
3. Active indicator — shows current location
4. User menu — secondary, at bottom

```
+---------------------------+
|  [> My Team ▼]        [»] |   ← Team selector + collapse toggle
|                           |
|  Navigation               |   ← Section heading
|                           |
|  ▎[▪] Issues              |   ← Active (Issues) — accent bar + highlight
|                           |
|  [▪] Projects             |   ← Inactive
|                           |
|  [▪] Cycles               |   ← Inactive
|                           |
|  [▪] Settings             |   ← Inactive
|                           |
|                           |
|  ───────────────────────  |
|                           |
|  👤 Juan Lagoria          |   ← User menu
+---------------------------+

--- Collapsed state: ---

+--------+
| [»]    |   ← Expand toggle
|        |
| [▪]    |   ← Icon only, tooltip on hover
|        |
| [▪]    |
|        |
| [▪]    |
|        |
| [▪]    |
|        |
| ────── |
|        |
| 👤     |   ← Icon only
+--------+
```

*Legend: [{Button}] [Input] [Link] [#Heading] [>Dropdown] [Avatar] [Icon]*

## Components & Affordances

| Element | DS Component | Behavior | Edge Cases |
|---------|-------------|----------|------------|
| Sidebar container | — | Fixed width, `overflow-y: auto` | Scroll if nav items exceed viewport height |
| Collapse toggle | IconButton | Toggles sidebar width, saves preference to UI Store | On mobile, collapse is default; toggle becomes hamburger |
| Team selector | Dropdown | Click → dropdown with team list → switch team reloads route | Single-team: hide or show as static label |
| Nav link (inactive) | NavLink (default variant) | `aria-current="false"`, click → navigate to route | — |
| Nav link (active) | NavLink (active variant) | `aria-current="page"`, left accent bar visible | Active for exact match AND child routes (e.g., `/issues/123` keeps Issues highlighted) |
| Nav link (collapsed) | NavLink (collapsed variant) | Icon only visible, label hidden, tooltip on hover | — |
| Nav section heading | — | Static `<h2>` text | Hidden in collapsed state |
| User menu button | Avatar + button | Click → dropdown: "Profile", "Log out" | On logout → redirect to `/login` |

## Data Display

N/A — sidebar is navigation, not data display.

## Content & Microcopy Intent

| Slot | Intent | Notes |
|------|--------|-------|
| "Navigation" | Section heading for primary nav links | Hidden when empty or single section; collapsed hides visually |
| "Issues" | Navigate to issue list | Icon: `▪` (list/bullet icon) |
| "Projects" | Navigate to project list | Icon: `▪` (folder/board icon) |
| "Cycles" | Navigate to cycles list | Icon: `▪` (cycle/target icon) |
| "Settings" | Navigate to settings page | Icon: `▪` (gear icon) |
| Team name in dropdown | Identifies current team context | — |
| User name at bottom | Identifies logged-in user | — |

## States

### Populated (Default) — Expanded

Full sidebar as shown in the ASCII sketch above. All nav links visible with active route highlighted.

### Populated — Collapsed

Sidebar reduced to icon-only (56px). Nav links show icons only with tooltips. Active indicator still visible as left accent bar. User menu shows avatar only.

### Loading

Sidebar skeleton: grey bars at nav link positions, no interaction until store hydrates.

```
+---------------------------+
|  [==== team ====]         |
|                           |
|  ======== section ======  |
|                           |
|  ▎ [==== skeleton ====]   |
|                           |
|  [==== skeleton ====]     |
|                           |
|  [==== skeleton ====]     |
|                           |
|  [==== skeleton ====]     |
|                           |
|  ───────────────────────  |
|                           |
|  ⬤                        |
+---------------------------+
```

### Error

N/A — sidebar is structural; errors in data-fetching are handled by the page content, not the nav.

### Empty

N/A — nav links are defined statically in route config, not fetched.

## Responsive

| Breakpoint | Changes |
|------------|---------|
| Desktop (>1024px) | Expanded sidebar (240px) by default, collapsible |
| Tablet (768-1024px) | Collapsed (56px) by default, expandable via toggle; overlay mode |
| Mobile (<768px) | Hidden by default; hamburger button in header opens sidebar as overlay with backdrop |

## Accessibility — Screen Composition

| Concern | Implementation |
|---------|----------------|
| Landmarks | `<aside aria-label="Main navigation">` |
| Heading order | Section heading (`<h2>`) only when content sections exist; page has its own `<h1>` in `<main>` |
| Reading / Focus order | Sidebar first in DOM (before `<main>`), focus order: toggle → team selector → nav links → user menu; collapsed state skips hidden items from Tab order |
| Accessible names | Collapse/expand toggle: `aria-label="Collapse sidebar"` / `aria-label="Expand sidebar"` |
| Keyboard operability | Tab through nav links, Enter to navigate, Arrow keys not needed (no sub-navigation) |
| Target size | Each nav link row ≥44px height for touch target reservation; icons in collapsed state ≥24×24 CSS px |
| Focus not obscured | Active indicator bar is left-side only, does not overlap focused element |
| Non-color intent | Active state uses left accent bar + bold text + icon, not colour alone |

*Defer to design-system: pixel contrast, focus-appearance, per-component target-size/keyboard.*
